 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Most rural families and many town families in Cameroon cook with firewood or charcoal. A firewood crisis is a serious shortage of wood for fuel.\nCauses: rapid population growth; cutting trees faster than they grow; clearing land for farms; drought and desertification in the North; poverty (gas and electricity are too expensive); wasteful three-stone fires.\nManifestations (signs): women and children walk farther to find wood; the price of firewood and charcoal rises; trucks bring wood from far away; bare land around towns like Maroua and Garoua.\nConsequences: desertification and soil erosion, less rain, loss of animals, children missing school to fetch wood, smoke that harms the lungs.\nSolutions: plant fast-growing trees (woodlots), improved (energy-saving) stoves, using cooking gas and solar cookers, biogas, laws against illegal cutting, teaching people to save wood.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "x": "improved stoves"
  },
  "problem": "How do {x} help to solve the firewood crisis?",
  "steps": [
   "An improved stove keeps the heat around the pot instead of letting it escape.",
   "It cooks the same food with much less wood."
  ],
  "answer": "They use less wood, so fewer trees are cut.",
  "checks": []
 },
